# Per-scenario rubric for the LLM judge layer.
#
# Four criteria per step, weights summing to 1.0: map_quality 0.40 / specificity 0.25
# / justification 0.20 / uncertainty 0.15.
#
# WHY map_quality carries the most weight here: this scenario's axis is REACH INTO TWO
# DIFFERENT KINDS OF DEPENDENT. One kind calls the class once from the middle of an
# unrelated job; the other never calls it at all and only holds a stored reference to one
# of its records, declared by a lowercase symbol the framework resolves. A search over the
# class name prints the first kind and cannot print the second.
#
# WHY specificity NO LONGER demands an enclosing routine for every dependent: the cycle-2
# rubric and ask both did, and a declared link sits in no routine. The sense arm reached all
# seven declared-link rows and then collapsed them into a single unlocated bullet, scoring
# mentioned 7 / cited 1. The unit demanded here is a file:line per dependent; the routine is
# demanded only where one exists.
#
# TWO steps, matching the cycle-3 two-step probe. The cycle-2 rubric is kept at
# discourse.rubric.yaml.mixed-22row.bak; the seven-step one at
# discourse.rubric.yaml.briefed-7step.bak.
#
# Step names MUST match scenarios/discourse.yaml exactly (the judge pairs by name).

audience: 'An AI coding agent that will use this answer to safely rework the Discourse category

  class - the container topics are filed under, carrying its own permissions, settings and

  hierarchy. Score for that agent, not a human reader and not a docs page. A perfect answer

  leaves the agent able to change that class knowing two things: how the rest of the system

  gets hold of one of these records when all it holds is the human-readable path out of a

  URL - traced through the routines that make that path up - and every other place that

  would have to be reviewed or changed with the class, each pinned to an exact file:line

  with the consequence of the change on that place stated. The dependents that matter come

  in two kinds and the answer must reach both. Some are doing an unrelated job - seeding a

  new site, composing a notification subject, polling a feed, initialising an import,

  explaining a tag exclusion - and reach for the class once in the middle of it. Others

  never reach for it at all: they are record types that hold a stored reference to one of

  these, declared once as a lowercase association and resolved by the framework, so the

  class name is nowhere in their file. A weak answer sweeps the obviously category-named

  neighbours and stops; collapses a set of record types into one line of names with a

  shared reason and no location on any of them; or gives file:line with nothing said about

  what would break - which leaves the agent knowing where the name appears and not what its

  change would do.

  '
steps:
- name: Map the category contract
  criteria:
    map_quality:
      weight: 0.4
      question: 'Is the slug-path resolution path traced end to end as one connected path, rather

        than listed as places the class is mentioned? A strong answer reaches the

        class-level entry point every lookup bottoms out in, the trailing-id variant, the

        one-level lookup the hierarchy walk is built from, the hierarchy walk itself, the

        HTTP front door, the rename path that keeps a stored slug in step, and the

        retired-path redirect. Credit is for showing how they connect, not for the count.

        Could the next step act from this map with small targeted lookups rather than a

        fresh exploration?

        '
    specificity:
      weight: 0.25
      question: 'Does every place carry an exact file:line AND the name of the routine it lives

        in? A bare filename is not specific. A file:line with no routine named around it

        is not specific - the maintainer asked whose code it is, not where the character

        offset falls. A routine named without the file:line where it is defined is not

        specific either.

        '
    justification:
      weight: 0.2
      question: 'Does each place carry one phrase on what it contributes to the resolution path -

        which input form it accepts, what it disambiguates, what it falls back to, why it

        refuses? Do the closing sentences say what a rework must preserve in terms of

        behaviour, rather than restating the method names?

        '
    uncertainty:
      weight: 0.15
      question: 'Does the answer separate what it verified by reading from what it inferred from a

        name? Guessing at a fallback it never opened is worse than saying it did not

        check. Is completeness claimed without saying how it was established?

        '
- name: Audit every dependent of the category contract
  criteria:
    map_quality:
      weight: 0.4
      question: 'THE DISCRIMINATOR. Does the audit reach BOTH kinds of dependent, or only the

        kind a reader working outward from the class itself would find? The first kind is

        code in the middle of an unrelated job - seeding a new site, composing a

        notification subject line, polling an external feed, initialising an import

        uploader, explaining why a tag was excluded - that reaches for the class exactly

        once. The second kind never reaches for it: a record type that stores a reference

        to one of these, declared as a lowercase association or through a join, so its

        file never writes the class name. An answer that is strong on the first kind and

        silent on the second has found what a text search finds and stopped. Breadth

        across areas is being measured, and missing a whole area is a regression shipped.

        Re-listing the class''s own surface, or the join models named after it, is not

        this question.

        '
    specificity:
      weight: 0.25
      question: 'Does EVERY dependent carry its own exact file:line - the line that makes the

        call, or the line that declares the stored reference? Several record types named

        together on one line as a set that shares a reason is the failure this criterion

        exists to catch: however correct the shared reason is, it is one item, not a set

        of located dependents, and it should be scored as one. Where the dependency sits

        inside a routine, is that routine named? A bare filename does not count.

        '
    justification:
      weight: 0.2
      question: 'Does each dependent carry one phrase on what that place would start getting wrong

        if the class changed under it? The consequence must be about that place''s own job

        - what breaks for the site being seeded, the email being addressed, the feed being

        polled, the draft waiting to be published, the timer waiting to fire, the webhook

        waiting to be filtered - not a restatement of the line of code.

        '
    uncertainty:
      weight: 0.15
      question: 'Does the answer say how it convinced itself the audit is exhaustive, and name

        where it is likely still thin? An unqualified claim of completeness over a

        codebase this size is overconfidence. Flagging areas it could not reach within

        budget is worth more than a confident list that quietly stops.

        '
